destroy_kokkos() is what nulls the base pointer (src/KOKKOS/memory_kokkos.h:83-88 and :271-281), and that nulling is exactly what makes the base destructor's memory->destroy(eflags)/orient/dorient (src/RIGID/fix_rigid_small.cpp:498-500) a no-op.  But eflags/orient/dorient are allocated in grow_arrays (fix_rigid_small_kokkos.cpp:1670-1677) with the flag values current at that time, and src/RIGID/fix_rigid_small.cpp:1777 `extended = orientflag = dorientflag = 0;` re-derives all three at the start of every setup_bodies_static(), which reinitflag re-runs on each subsequent run.

